Here is a first-date drinks plan built around Dante West Village, 551 Hudson St (corner of Perry), New York, NY 10014.

Brief: nice first date, drinks-forward. Scope: the West Village within a 10-minute walk of Dante West Village. Checked September 2026.

## 1 The Decision Rule

Which bar you should pick depends on what night you go, because the binding constraint in these four blocks is not quality — it is the door. Almost every good room here is walk-in, and a first date that opens with 30 minutes in a line is a first date that burns its best material on the sidewalk.

| If you're going | Go to | Address | Walk from Dante | Why |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| **Tue–Thu, arriving 6:30–7:30pm** | **Katana Kitten** | 531 Hudson St | ~2 min | Best drink-to-distance ratio in the neighborhood. Walk-in, and at that hour on a weeknight you get seats. |
| **Fri–Sat, or arriving after 8pm** | **Guzzle** (ground floor of Sip & Guzzle) | 29 Cornelia St | ~10 min | The one nearby room that takes a reservation AND is described as staying calm. Don't gamble on a walk-in on a weekend. |
| **Tue–Sat and you can be at the door at 5:00pm** | **Angel's Share** | 45 Grove St | ~8 min | The best room of the three. Opening time is the only reliable way in. |

Walk times are estimates from 551 Hudson St at a normal pace.

## 2 The Three Primary Options

### Katana Kitten — 531 Hudson St

One block south of Dante, same side of Hudson. Japanese-American cocktail bar from Masahiro Urushido; a fixture on the North America's 50 Best Bars list. Highballs, Japanese whisky, Japanese movie posters on the wall, a real food menu, two floors.

- **Hours:** Sun 2pm–12am; Mon–Fri 4pm–2am; Sat 2pm–2am [Verified — Yelp listing, updated July 2026]
- **Reservations:** none. Walk-in. [Verified — venue has no booking platform listed]
- **Register:** lively, not hushed. Energy without a shouting match before 9pm. [Likely — consistent across The Infatuation's West Village guide and review aggregates]
- **First-date fit:** high. Good drinks give you something to talk about, the food menu gives you an exit ramp if one drink turns into three hours, and one block from Dante means no transit negotiation.
- **Failure mode:** after 9pm on a weekend it fills and gets loud. Arrive by 7:30 or choose something else.

### Guzzle (Sip & Guzzle) — 29 Cornelia St

Bi-level bar from Shingo Gokan and Steve Schneider. Ground floor is **Guzzle** — Schneider's room, classics and familiar drinks done right. Basement is **Sip** — Gokan's five-seat bar, technique-driven, designed around the Kanrin Maru.

- **Reservations:** Resy, both floors. Walk-ins welcomed. [Verified — sipandguzzlenyc.com/reservations]
- **Register:** The Infatuation singles it out as one that "doesn't get too loud or hectic" compared with its competitors. [Verified — quoted in their West Village bars guide]
- **First-date fit:** highest of any room here, because it removes the door risk. A confirmed 7:00pm reservation means you walk in and sit down, which is worth more on a first date than any cocktail.
- **Which floor:** book **Guzzle** upstairs for a first date. **Sip** downstairs is five seats and a fixed pace — that is a second- or third-date room, and a five-seat bar leaves you nowhere to go if the conversation stalls.
- **Trade-off:** ~10 minutes from Dante. On a first date a 10-minute walk is an asset, not a cost — walking side by side removes eye-contact pressure and hands you something to look at.

### Angel's Share — 45 Grove St

Reopened in the West Village after leaving its East Village home. Japanese speakeasy, behind a door off a restaurant. Precision cocktails, jazz, ornate wallpaper.

- **Hours:** Tue–Sat 5:00pm–12:00am. Closed Sunday and Monday. [Verified — Yelp listing, updated September 2026]
- **Door policy:** walk-in only; party maximum 4; no split parties; **no standing** [Verified — venue policy, cited in The Infatuation and Time Out]
- **Why the no-standing rule matters:** if they let you in, you have a seat. Nobody is crowding behind you. That is the single most date-friendly room policy in the West Village.
- **The catch:** the same rule caps the room, so the wait is unpredictable and there is nowhere to wait. Be at the door at 5:00pm Tuesday or Wednesday and the wait drops close to zero. [Likely — arriving at open is the standard recommendation for capacity-capped walk-in rooms; this one is stated across venue writeups]
- **First-date fit:** excellent once inside; risky as a plan. Treat it as Plan A only if you can start at 5, otherwise as a bonus stop.

## 3 Should You Drink at Dante Itself?

Reasonable, with a caveat. Dante West Village is a Negroni institution and the outdoor seating on Hudson is the best in the immediate radius.

- **Hours:** daily until 12am; brunch 10am–4pm weekends and holidays; dinner service from 5pm Sat–Sun [Verified — dante-nyc.com]
- **Reservations:** tables on Resy. **Bar seats are first-come, first-served and cannot be reserved.** [Verified — dante-nyc.com]
- **The caveat:** booking a table turns a drinks date into a dinner date — more commitment than a first date needs, and harder to end after 50 minutes. Taking the bar lottery on a Friday means you might be standing.
- **When it works:** a 5:00–6:30pm outdoor drink on a weekday. Bright room, low stakes, you can see each other, and you can walk one block to Katana Kitten if you want a second.

## 4 Second Stop — Pick It Before You Leave the House

Improvising the second bar in front of someone you met an hour ago is how you end up at whatever has an open door. Choose one now.

| Second stop | Address | Walk | Best for |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| **Love Thy Neighbor** | 55 Christopher St | ~8 min | Japanese-inspired lounge in a subterranean sandstone room. The step up in intimacy that a going-well first date wants. |
| **Employees Only** | 510 Hudson St | ~3 min | Back toward Dante. Opens 6pm, runs to 4am Mon–Sat; #45 on North America's 50 Best Bars 2026. Go before 9pm or it's shoulder-to-shoulder. |
| **Mezzrow** | 163 W 10th St | ~8 min | Live jazz in a basement. Sun–Thu admission includes a same-evening pass to Smalls at 183 W 10th. Use this when you want a second act that isn't more talking. |
| **Anton's** | 570 Hudson St | ~1 min | One block north of Dante. European-American café and wine bar if the drink turns into hunger. |
| **Bar Pisellino** | 52 Grove St | ~9 min | Negronis and sidewalk people-watching from the Via Carota team. Open 8am–11pm daily, no reservations. Best before 6pm — after that the line runs down the block. |

Mezzrow hours: Mon–Thu 6pm–12:30am; Fri–Sat 6pm–2am; Sun 3pm–1:30am [Verified — mezzrow.com]. Smalls is listed at a $10 cover plus one-drink minimum, but that figure reads dated — confirm at smallslive.com before you count on it. [Guessing — the number appears in an aggregator, not the venue]

## 5 What to Skip on a First Date Here

- **Bar Pisellino after 6pm** — the room is ten feet wide and the line stretches down Grove. Great bar, wrong hour.
- **The Garret, 296 Bleecker St** — described as getting "extremely loud and busy." You will not hear each other.
- **Marie's Crisis, 59 Grove St** — a basement show-tunes piano bar, and a joy. But nobody talks, and it's cash-only. Save it for a fourth date.
- **Little Branch, 20 7th Ave S** — dark basement, live jazz, unmarked door. It is a third-date room, not a first-date room: too dim to read a face, and the capacity cap means waits.
- **White Horse Tavern, 567 Hudson St** — across the street from Dante and historic, but the crowd skews tourist.
- **Via Carota / I Sodi** — outstanding, and both are dinner with a wait. Wrong shape for a drinks date.
- **Julius', Cubbyhole, Marie's Crisis** — all cash-only. Worth knowing before you're at the register.

## 6 Timing and Logistics

- **Best night:** Tuesday through Thursday. **Best arrival:** 6:30–7:30pm.
- **Friday and Saturday:** every walk-in room within four blocks of Dante has a line by 8pm. If you must go on a weekend, the Resy reservation at Guzzle is not optional — it's the plan.
- **Sunday/Monday:** Angel's Share is closed; Employees Only is closed Sunday. Katana Kitten and Dante both run 7 days.
- **Getting there:** Christopher St–Sheridan Sq (1 train) is ~6 minutes from 551 Hudson. 14th St (A/C/E, L) is ~10 minutes north.
- **The bail:** one drink at a walk-in bar, no reservation to honor, no food ordered. Say goodnight at the corner of Hudson and Perry. Build the plan so this costs nothing.

## 7 The One-Line Version

Tuesday through Thursday: Katana Kitten at 7:00pm, one block from Dante, with Love Thy Neighbor held in reserve. Friday or Saturday: book Guzzle on Resy and walk the ten minutes.

